# Manual REST Client requests for POST /classes/:id/enrolments and POST /enrolments/:id/withdraw (VS Code REST Client).
# Sign in with an approved student review account of REVIEW_ACCOUNTS in apps/backend/.env: set the email and code below.
# Codes are read from the backend log when RESEND_API_KEY is unset. Set `classId` to a class that hasn't started
# (GET /classes?date=YYYY-MM-DD lists them).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
@email = student@example.com
@code = 345678
@classId = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000

### Request a sign-in code (expects 202)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/email/code
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "locale": "pt-BR"
}

### Sign in (expects 200 with accessToken)
# @name session
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/email/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "code": "{{code}}"
}

###
@token = {{session.response.body.accessToken}}

### Request a seat (expects 201 with { id, classId, status: "pending", requestedAt }; the flag is required only when the class's discipline has a cancellation rule; a full class is accepted too)
# @name enrolment
POST {{baseUrl}}/classes/{{classId}}/enrolments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "acceptCancellationRule": true
}

###
@enrolmentId = {{enrolment.response.body.id}}

### The class now carries the caller's enrolment (expects myEnrolment: { id, status: "pending", requestedAt })
GET {{baseUrl}}/classes/{{classId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Requesting the same class again while the request is open (expects 409 enrolment.alreadyOpen)
POST {{baseUrl}}/classes/{{classId}}/enrolments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "acceptCancellationRule": true
}

### Without accepting the rule of a discipline that has one (expects 422 enrolment.rule.notAccepted)
POST {{baseUrl}}/classes/{{classId}}/enrolments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### An unknown or malformed class (expects 404 class.notFound)
POST {{baseUrl}}/classes/not-a-uuid/enrolments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "acceptCancellationRule": true
}

### A cancelled class (expects 409 class.cancelled) or one that has started (expects 409 class.started)
POST {{baseUrl}}/classes/{{classId}}/enrolments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "acceptCancellationRule": true
}

### As an instructor or an admin (expects 403 enrolment.role.notStudent), with an account that isn't approved (expects 403 user.status.notApproved) or without a token (expects 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/classes/{{classId}}/enrolments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "acceptCancellationRule": true
}

### Withdraw the pending request (expects 200 with { id, classId, status: "withdrawn", requestedAt })
POST {{baseUrl}}/enrolments/{{enrolmentId}}/withdraw
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Withdrawing it again (expects 409 enrolment.notPending); a class that has started answers 409 class.started
POST {{baseUrl}}/enrolments/{{enrolmentId}}/withdraw
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### An unknown, malformed or another person's enrolment (expects 404 enrolment.notFound)
POST {{baseUrl}}/enrolments/not-a-uuid/withdraw
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Request the class again after the withdrawal (expects 201 with a new pending enrolment)
POST {{baseUrl}}/classes/{{classId}}/enrolments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "acceptCancellationRule": true
}
